{"team":"ATL","col":"#FF525B","identity":"run-heavy","funnel":"run-funnel","plays_pg":62.0,"adot":7.9,"report_html":"<div class=\"report\"><h2>Built to Run</h2><p>Run identity is the through-line here: ATL call pass on <strong>-7%</strong> of snaps relative to what the situation expects (league -2%), and when they get ahead they lean even harder on the ground \u2014 just 33% pass on early downs with a lead. This is a ball-control operation built to shorten games.</p><h3>The Offensive Blueprint</h3><p>Their run game attacks the perimeter \u2014 <strong>32% of carries hit the edge</strong> (league ~25%), an outside-zone lean that rewards speed backs and can boom for chunk gains.</p><p>They live in the shotgun (81% of snaps vs ~68%) \u2014 a spread, pass-oriented structure.</p><p><strong>Kyle Pitts</strong> is a genuine centerpiece, not an afterthought \u2014 <strong>18%</strong> of targets (league ~15%).</p><p>By the numbers it's an efficient unit \u2014 a 46% success rate (above the 44% average).</p><h3>In the Red Zone</h3><p>Inside the 20 they lean run-heavy, passing <strong>46%</strong> of the time, funnelling touchdown equity to <strong>Bijan Robinson</strong>. And with the TE commanding 18% of targets, <strong>Kyle Pitts</strong> is a live red-zone option too.</p><h2>Defense \u2014 The Run Comes Free</h2><p>They surrender <strong>124 rushing</strong> and <strong>229 passing</strong> yards per game (league ~120 / ~230). The run moves against them \u2014 <strong>target opposing RB1s</strong>.</p><p>They lock down opposing WR1s \u2014 just 52 rec yds/game (vs ~58); fade receiving props there.</p><p>They leak <strong>WR1 receiving TDs</strong> (0.47/game vs ~0.38) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><h2>The Betting Angles</h2><p>Bottom line: back <strong>Bijan Robinson</strong>'s rushing volume in favored/positive scripts; <strong>opposing RB1s</strong> smash on the ground and at the goal line.</p><p><em>Built on 2024\u201325 data; the profile rebuilds through the season as the current staff and roster set their own tendencies.</em></p></div>","depth":{"QB":[{"name":"Tua Tagovailoa","slot":"QB1","starter":true,"td":4,"props":{"Comp":18.64,"Att":27.43,"Pass Yds":207.47,"Pass TD":1.5,"INT":1.67,"Rush Yds":3.99},"d":{"completions":18.64,"attempts":27.43,"pass_yards":207.47,"pass_td":1.5,"interceptions":1.67,"rush_att":1.22,"rush_yards":3.99}}],"RB":[{"name":"Bijan Robinson","slot":"RB1","starter":true,"td":46,"props":{"Rush Att":18.78,"Rush Yds":90.15,"Tgt":7.99,"Rec":6.23,"Rec Yds":54.28},"d":{"rush_att":18.78,"rush_yards":90.15,"targets":7.99,"receptions":6.23,"rec_yards":54.28,"rec_td":0.2}},{"name":"Brian Robinson","slot":"RB2","starter":true,"td":17,"props":{"Rush Att":6.1,"Rush Yds":25.58,"Tgt":2.04,"Rec":1.66,"Rec Yds":12.81},"d":{"rush_att":6.1,"rush_yards":25.58,"targets":2.04,"receptions":1.66,"rec_yards":12.81,"rec_td":0.06}}],"WR":[{"name":"Drake London","slot":"WR1","starter":true,"td":28,"props":{"Tgt":10.19,"Rec":6.46,"Rec Yds":81.72,"Rec TD":0.32},"d":{"targets":10.19,"receptions":6.46,"rec_yards":81.72,"rec_td":0.32}},{"name":"Jahan Dotson","slot":"WR2","starter":true,"td":16,"props":{"Tgt":4.25,"Rec":2.1,"Rec Yds":25.76,"Rec TD":0.17},"d":{"targets":4.25,"receptions":2.1,"rec_yards":25.76,"rec_td":0.17}},{"name":"Olamide Zaccheaus","slot":"WR3","starter":true,"td":13,"props":{"Tgt":4.49,"Rec":2.9,"Rec Yds":32.89,"Rec TD":0.14},"d":{"targets":4.49,"receptions":2.9,"rec_yards":32.89,"rec_td":0.14}},{"name":"Zachariah Branch","slot":"WR4","starter":false,"td":9,"props":{"Tgt":3.35,"Rec":1.85,"Rec Yds":23.46,"Rec TD":0.1},"d":{"targets":3.35,"receptions":1.85,"rec_yards":23.46,"rec_td":0.1}},{"name":"Chris Blair","slot":"WR5","starter":false,"td":9,"props":{"Tgt":2.7,"Rec":1.44,"Rec Yds":17.47,"Rec TD":0.09},"d":{"targets":2.7,"receptions":1.44,"rec_yards":17.47,"rec_td":0.09}}],"TE":[{"name":"Kyle Pitts","slot":"TE1","starter":true,"td":21,"props":{"Tgt":9.59,"Rec":6.2,"Rec Yds":76.96,"Rec TD":0.25},"d":{"target